WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.068
The House Ways and Means Committee

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.304
now has access to six years

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.473
of Donald Trump's tax returns.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.741
What are they going to do with them?

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:07.974
Yeah,

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.376
so they have to decide now

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.910
that they have access, how exactly

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.379
they're going to handle the returns.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.047
That could actually be a main point

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:14.647
in a meeting

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.348
they're going to have

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.250
with legal counsel tomorrow.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.318
The big thing, though, is

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.319
it's still unclear

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:19.853
if the public

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.421
will actually get to see these

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.656
six years of Trump's tax returns.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.359
We know that the public and all of us

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.261
definitely won't get immediate access

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:28.962
to them.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:29.896
It's possible

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:30.663
they could be released

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.698
sometime down the road.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.065
Of course,

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.233
that could impact

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.401
Trump's presidential bid

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.603
that he's announced for 20, 24.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.371
Trump has already for years

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:38.972
repeatedly

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.807
refused to release his tax returns

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.343
throughout 2016 2020 campaigns,

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.245
even throughout his presidency.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.080
We did get a glimpse of information

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.049
from the New York Times back in 2020

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.150
they found that Trump

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.352
paid no federal income taxes at all

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.987
beginning in 2000.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.523
So we could see potentially in the future

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.157
depending on what

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:57.724
the House Ways

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.192
and Means Committee decides

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.660
to do with these returns.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.395
What else might be buried

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.431
in six years of Trump's tax returns.

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:05.298
But it's not anything

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.200
the public is going to see any soon.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.235
And this committee has just weeks

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.670
before they wrap up

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.438
to really decide

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.605
how they want to handle them as well

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.239
John. All right.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.974
Jessica Snyder, thank you so much.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.375
With us

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.376
now is investigative

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.378
reporter and Trump biographer David Cay.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.380
Johnson, author of The Big Cheat

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.981
How Donald Trump Fleeced America

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.117
and Enriched Himself and His Family.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:24.551
So, David,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.752
the House Ways and Means Committee,

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.953
they don't have much time

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:27.987
to investigate

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.322
the former president's taxes

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.223
if they want.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.758
Do Democrats only control this committee

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.426
for another month or so?

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.495
So what are the most immediate questions

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.096
that could be answered

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:36.963
by these documents?

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.867
Well, they could tell us definitively

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.001
whether Donald,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.304
on his tax returns, manipulated

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.638
the value of assets

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:46.973
he was depreciating

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.808
when you own an asset like a building,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.376
you get to write off

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.378
part of the cost of it each year

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.180
and it saves your tax dollars.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.615
And we know from The New York

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.750
Times investigation four years ago

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.220
that Trump manipulated values

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.456
all over the place to deal with loans

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.025
and insurance documents.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.861
So that would be one of the first things

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.595
to look for.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.163
And second,

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.565
to look for numbers that don't match up.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.400
You claim to have X amount of money

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.002
in the bank in a particular account

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.038
at the end of an entity.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.107
Donald has 500 entities,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.709
and the amount of money

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.711
you have the next year doesn't match up.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.880
It should be exactly to close out

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.214
the start of the next year.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:29.582
But they

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.383
don't have much time

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.050
to look at that,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.453
if that's what they want to do.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.787
So the tax returns and questions

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.822
are primarily

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.523
from the period

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.191
when Donald Trump was president,

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.492
when he was in the White House.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.560
So how do you think

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.163
that affects the investigation?

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.565
Well, I'd be much more interested

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.300
John, in seeing the tax returns

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.102
before he became president,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.704
because there's testimony in the ongoing

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:52.839
New York City

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.207
trial on tax

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.309
cheating by the Trump organization

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.978
that they cleaned up their behavior

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.580
once Donald Trump

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.348
arrived in the White House.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.349
But the issue

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.751
the committee was concerned

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:05.752
about was Donald

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.420
Trump's repeated claims

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.557
that he was persecuted by the IRS

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.824
because he's a Christian.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.425
Never mind

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.660
that he has called in a book

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.062
Christians Fools and Schmucks and Idiots

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.430
and has declared

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.631
repeatedly his life's

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.533
philosophy is revenge,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.969
which is inherently anti Christian.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:23.803
That was

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.171
the issue was the president

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.005
of the United States

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.707
and a presidential candidate

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.410
being treated properly by the IRS?

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.778
That's an issue

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.813
I can imagine the Democrats might

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.649
the Republicans might want to get into,

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.251
depending on how facts

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.252
turn out in the future.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.221
Not likely, but possible

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.288
since they're always trying

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.556
to beat up the IRS.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.091
So the chair of the House Ways and Means

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:45.692
Committee, Richie Neal,

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.593
declined to say

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.894
whether they would release

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.796
any of these returns publicly.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.631
Do you think any of these will

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.365
see the light of day

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.134
Well, I hope so.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.436
First and foremost,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.004
Ricky Neil is very concerned

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.106
about a section of the tax code

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.041
that makes tax returns confidential.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.543
They used to be public record

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.678
100 years ago, they were public,

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.346
but they're not.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.981
Now, there are procedures

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.948
by which the committee

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.450
can put the tax returns

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.818
into the public record.

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:14.287
He's having a meeting with his caucus

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.154
on the committee.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.422
And I think one of the things

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.091
they're certain to discuss is,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.125
is there a way for them

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.327
to put this into the congressional record

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.929
so that it's always there

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.564
and people on the outside

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.966
can basically crowdsource an audit?

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.801
Look, the former president's

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.003
legal team has fought for years,

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.970
so as a former president

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.005
to keep this secret.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.173
You've reported on him extensive valley.

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.143
Why do you think he worked so hard

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.279
to keep these from going public?

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.015
Because Donald's a tax cheat.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:42.282
I mean,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.883
I've established in the public record

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.286
previously he cheated on sales taxes.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.054
He cheated on payroll taxes,

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.322
actually even cheated

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.657
not a roulette players

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.325
at one of his casinos.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.226
And The New York Times

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.027
investigation

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.728
that they said was inspired

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.130
by my reporting

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.131
four years ago

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.867
showed very, very calculated

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:04.003
income tax cheating by the Trump family.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:04.704
It also involved

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.939
gift tax and estate tax cheating.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.007
That's who Trump is.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.142
He's done this his whole life.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.977
He's cheated on investors and workers.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:14.881
And as I said, even some gamblers So,

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.382
of course, the tax returns,

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.718
if fully audited, are going to show

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.953
that he cheated on his income taxes.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:21.854
David Cay Johnston,

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.257
thank you for your insight.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:24.957
Thank you, John.

